## Counter
// A button that counts its clicks:  the smallest app there is.
// What's where, top to bottom:
//   a counter:  its count, counting up, and its drawing
//   the app:  one counter, drawn
//   start
//   tests


## A counter -- in the outline style:  its name, then what's true of it
// A view:  each counter is its own element on the page.
// The Counter notebook, `@spell/notebooks/Counter`, imports it, and tries it out.
<spell-view "counter">
	<property "count">a number</>
	// a new counter starts at 0
	<action "create it">set its count to 0</>
	<action "count up">set its count to its count + 1</>

	// a button saying how many times it's been clicked:  a click counts up
	<draw><button onClick={count up}>Clicked {its count} times</button></draw>
</spell-view>


## The app:  one counter, drawn
<spell-app "counter app">
	<property "counter">a new counter</>

	<spell>
		- to draw it:
			return <div class="Counter">{draw its counter}</div>
	</spell>
</spell-app>


## Start
<spell>
	start counter app
</spell>


## Tests
<spell>
	to test counting
		set the counter to a new counter
		the count of the counter should be 0
		count up of the counter
		count up of the counter
		the count of the counter should be 2
</spell>
